  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical support Limitless - Innovation Support IFRC Solferino Academy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the success from the Limitless programme, the IFRC SA is seeking support for setting up a second phase of the programme, Limitless 2.0. The idea is to build gains achieved during the first implementation of Limitless and to grow the initiative into a major global impact effort that is powered by local solutions, enables new forms of volunteering, and attracts new people/ partners, ways of working and solutions to the RCRC network.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IFRC Solferino Academy (IFRC SA) designed a programme with a capability-strengthening approach to identify young innovators with ideas and build a support system for them. Hence the IFRC Limitless Youth Innovation Academy was initiated. Within the programme, the IFRC SA calls out all young Red Cross Red Crescent volunteers and staff to see if they had a project in mind to help their community. If they want to bring that idea to life, then they can apply and join the IFRC Youth Innovation Academy.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Volunteers and staff of RC National Societies</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Within the second phase, Limitless will focus on promoting innovations to address the climate and environmental crises, an issue of global passion for our youth and volunteers. To achieve this, in collaboration with numerous partners, they will reach out to our global network to surface and support high-potential ideas and initiatives driven by our volunteers. The overall aim is to support over 1,000 youth-led innovations in 150 countries and to impact the lives of more than 1 million community members. Additionally, they will also further shortlist 50 projects that possess extremely high potential for impact, who will receive more focused and advanced mentorship and guidance and additional funding to develop their projects. This project is designed to facilitate a technical support to the IFRC programme.</narrative>
  </description>
